---
import LegalLayout from "../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { getTranslations } from "../../i18n";

const lang = "en";
const t = getTranslations(lang);
---

<LegalLayout
  title={t.meta.cookiesTitle}
  description="SliceBill Cookie Policy — what cookies we use and how to manage them."
  lang={lang}
  lastUpdated="November 20, 2026"
>
  <h2>1. What Are Cookies?</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small text files stored on your device by your web browser when you visit a website. They are widely used to make websites work reliably, maintain security, and remember user preferences.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Cookies and Local Storage We Use</h2>
  <p>SliceBill (<code>slicebill.app</code> and the web app <code>web.slicebill.app</code>) uses only strictly necessary technical storage required for app operation and security:</p>

  <h3>Essential Cookies and Browser Storage</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Firebase Authentication session</strong> — stores your sign-in state in browser storage (IndexedDB / cookies) so you remain authenticated across sessions.
      <br /><em>Duration: session / persistent login</em>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Offline browser storage (Hive CE &amp; Firestore IndexedDB cache)</strong> — stores local-only groups created without an account, language/theme/currency preferences, and pending offline edits until synced to the server.
      <br /><em>Duration: until you clear site data or delete groups in the app</em>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google reCAPTCHA Enterprise (Firebase App Check)</strong> — strictly necessary security cookies and attestation tokens on <code>web.slicebill.app</code> used exclusively to protect API endpoints from bots and abuse (never for advertising).
      <br /><em>Duration: session / per Google security policy</em>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>What We Do NOT Use</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Advertising or profiling cookies</li>
    <li>Third-party marketing analytics cookies (no Google Analytics, Meta Pixel, etc.)</li>
    <li>Social media tracking pixels</li>
    <li>Any cookies that track you across other websites</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Third-Party Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    SliceBill uses <strong>Google Firebase</strong> (authentication and database) and <strong>Google reCAPTCHA Enterprise</strong> (Firebase App Check bot protection). These mechanisms only set essential authentication and security tokens governed by <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you voluntarily send a tip on the web app ("Buy Me a Coffee"), redirecting to the <strong>Stripe</strong> Checkout gateway uses Stripe's essential security and checkout session cookies.
  </p>
  <p>
    Google Fonts is used to load the Inter typeface on this landing site from Google's CDN. Google may process standard font request headers (IP address, browser details).
  </p>

  <h2>4. Managing Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    You can control and delete cookies or site data through your browser settings. Please note that disabling essential cookies or IndexedDB will prevent signing in on <code>web.slicebill.app</code>, disable offline syncing, and prevent saving local groups.
  </p>
  <p>Browser cookie management guides:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/95647" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Chrome</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/cookies-information-websites-store-on-your-computer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Mozilla Firefox</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/105082" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Safari</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Cookie Policy to reflect changes in our practices. We will notify you by updating the "Last updated" date above.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    If you have questions about our use of cookies, contact us:<br />
    DARDAN SP. Z O.O.<br />
    Email: <a href="mailto:support@slicebill.app">support@slicebill.app</a>
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
